-- title:
--   Base-change maps from F⊗_{A[a]}B as A-algebra maps with prescribed value at a
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings with $B$ an $A$-algebra, let $a\in B$, and write $S=\mathrm{adjoin}_A\{a\}$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $B$ generated by $a$. Let $F$ be a commutative ring which is an $S$-algebra, and let $T$ be a commutative ring which is simultaneously an $A$-algebra, an $F$-algebra and an $S$-algebra, these structures being compatible in the sense that $T$ is a scalar tower over $S\to F\to T$ and over $A\to S\to T$. The assertion is that the type of bijections between, on the one hand, the $F$-algebra homomorphisms $F\otimes_S B\to T$ and, on the other hand, the subtype of those $A$-algebra homomorphisms $\varphi\colon B\to T$ satisfying $\varphi(a)=\mathrm{algebraMap}_{S,T}(a)$, where $a$ is regarded as the element of $S$ given by `Algebra.self_mem_adjoin_singleton`, is nonempty. Thus an explicit equivalence exists, but the statement records only its existence and does not name a particular one.
--
--   This is the base-change adjunction $\mathrm{Hom}_{F\text{-alg}}(F\otimes_S B,T)\cong\mathrm{Hom}_{S\text{-alg}}(B,T)$ for $S=A[a]$, combined with the observation that an $A$-algebra map out of $B$ is $S$-linear precisely when it sends $a$ to the prescribed image of $a$ in $T$. It is used in the study of the generic fibre of the moduli data attached to modular curves, in the computations of reducedness and of the rank of a fraction-field base change at full level and for $\Gamma_0$-type data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_nonempty_algHom_tensorProduct_adjoin_equiv_subtype_apply_eq.lean

